# Rust crates

- `oxidean-core`: shared types / pure domain — no SQL, no Axum.
- `oxidean-db`: migrations + `Database` API; all dialect branching stays here.
- `oxidean-api`: HTTP/RPC/auth/email; call `Database`, do not fork SQL per dialect.
- Prefer `Result` + structured errors; no `unwrap`/`expect` outside tests.
- Preserve auth gates (`require_verified`, admin, bootstrap). Destructive RPCs keep explicit confirmations.
- After RPC or shared DTO changes: `make rpc-gen` and keep `packages/api-client` in the same change.
- Tests: unit colocated; cross-cutting in `crates/*/tests/`. CI uses nextest (`--profile ci`).
- See [docs/CODE_PRACTICES.md](../../docs/CODE_PRACTICES.md) and `.agents/skills/rust-best-practices`.
